# The raw chain store. Untracked since 2026-11-22: Git LFS stores a complete
# new copy of a SQLite file on every push, which took the quota to 9.01GB of
# an included 10GB while the daily growth rate never changed. It is published
# as release assets instead and fetched with `python -m src.chain_release
# sync` -- see that module for the whole story.
#
# Two paths, because the store is two things: a small index file holding the
# prices and the record of which dates exist, and a directory of compressed
# monthly chain partitions beside it. Ignoring only the first would leave
# `git status` offering to commit the chains a month at a time.
#
# Ignored rather than merely deleted so a stray `git add` cannot put any of
# it back into the repository. Nothing here is LFS-tracked any more, so
# there would be nothing to soften a mistake.
database/schwab_database.db
database/schwab_database_chains/
database/*.partitioned.db
database/*.partitioned_chains/

# Temporary files from an interrupted fetch. src/chain_release.py writes
# beside the destination -- os.replace() is only atomic within one
# filesystem -- and unlinks on failure, but a killed process leaves one.
*.db.download

# Local-only databases. Point a local dev session at one of these via
# SCHWAB_DB_PATH so a live refresh never writes over the downloaded copy:
#
#   export SCHWAB_DB_PATH=database/local.db
#
database/local*.db
database/*.local.db
demo-data/

# Backups written by src/backfill_session_dates.py --apply. ~52MB of store
# plus the metric history, so an accidental `git add` would put a lot of
# binary into git proper -- painful to undo, and nothing in this repo is
# LFS-tracked any more to soften it. They are your undo for the
# relabelling; delete them once the result is verified and published.
*.pre-backfill
*.pre-backfill_chains/
